  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Magnesium levulinate and DNA-3-methyladenine glycosylase, mediated through Selgantolimod. This is supported by multiple paths indicating that Magnesium levulinate targets different proteins, including Keratin, Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A, and Plasma kallikrein, all of which are targets of Selgantolimod. Selgantolimod itself is known to interact with DNA-3-methyladenine glycosylase, implying a chain of interactions where Magnesium levulinate may influence the activity or expression of these intermediate proteins, which in turn affect DNA-3-methyladenine glycosylase. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.694) suggest a plausible biological connection, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible regulatory or enzymatic pathway, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Magnesium levulinate and DNA-3-methyladenine glycosylase.",
